[size=3][b]Version: next (xlibs 1.8.4, demonized 20250908)[/b][/size]
[size=3][b]GitHub: [url=https://github.com/damiansirbu-stalker/DiegeticControl]https://github.com/damiansirbu-stalker/DiegeticControl[/url][/b][/size]
[size=3][b]Changelog: [url=https://github.com/damiansirbu-stalker/DiegeticControl/blob/main/doc/changelog]doc/changelog[/url] | [url=https://github.com/damiansirbu-stalker/DiegeticControl/blob/main/doc/readme_ru.txt]На русском[/url] | [url=https://github.com/damiansirbu-stalker/DiegeticControl/issues]Bugs, suggestions[/url][/b][/size]

Anomaly has no way to control the volume of radios, megaphones, guitars, and harmonicas independently from the game's audio sliders. You can't turn down Duty propaganda without killing ambient sounds. DiegeticControl fixes this.

The mod hooks directly into the audio subsystems that play in-world sound: ph_sound for radios and megaphones, guitar_anim for campfire guitar, harmonica_anim for harmonica. Each source gets its own volume slider, enable/disable toggle, and where applicable a pause multiplier that controls silence between tracks or announcements.

A master volume multiplier sits on top of everything. All changes apply immediately through MCM.

Missing dependencies are handled gracefully. If you don't have the guitar or harmonica mods installed, those controls simply do nothing.

[line]

[size=3][b]Features:[/b][/size]

[size=2][b]Radios:[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Volume control for faction base radios and music
[*]Pause multiplier between tracks (longer silence or shorter)
[*]Enable/disable toggle
[/list]

[size=2][b]Megaphones:[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Volume control for Duty propaganda, Arena announcer, alarms
[*]Pause multiplier between announcements
[*]Enable/disable toggle
[/list]

[size=2][b]Guitar:[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Volume control for campfire guitar (requires Guitar Animation mod)
[*]Enable/disable toggle
[/list]

[size=2][b]Harmonica:[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Volume control for harmonica (requires Harmonica mod)
[*]Enable/disable toggle
[/list]

Master volume multiplier applied to all sources

[line]

[size=3][b]Requirements:[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Anomaly 1.5.3
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stalkeranomaly/mods/102]xlibs[/url]
[*]MCM
[*]Radio_Remastered or similar (for radio/megaphone control)
[*]Guitar Animation by Daiviey (optional, for guitar control)
[*]Harmonica by Daiviey (optional, for harmonica control)
[/list]

[size=3][b]Install (MO2):[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Install xlibs
[*]Install DiegeticControl
[*]Load order does not matter
[*]Configure via MCM
[/list]

[size=3][b]Uninstall (MO2):[/b][/size]
Disable or remove in MO2.

[line]

[size=3][b]Configuration:[/b][/size]
All settings in MCM under DiegeticControl. All defaults are 1.0 (unchanged from game behavior).

[size=3][b]Compatibility:[/b][/size]
Requires xlibs.
Runs on themrdemonized modded exes 20250908 or newer, or AOEngine v0.55 or newer.
The full feature set needs the latest demonized build. A feature that needs a newer build stays inactive on older exes.
Tested with GAMMA. Hooks into ph_sound, guitar_anim, and harmonica_anim. If those mods are not present the relevant controls are inactive. No base script modifications.

[line]

[size=3][b]Development:[/b][/size]
Written against X-Ray Monolith engine source, Demonized exes source code, and Anomaly 1.5.3 unpacked gamedata.
Code patterns and engine usage validated against established work by reputable GAMMA modders (Demonized, Vintar0, RavenAscendant, xcvb).
The code is validated in real time by a multi-stage pipeline: luacheck, selene, tree-sitter AST analysis, contract rules, cross-file dependency resolution, cyclomatic complexity analysis, crash and vulnerability pattern detection, lua54 integration testing with X-Ray engine stubs, gitleaks secret scanning.
Full report in doc/test-report.log.

[size=3][b]FAQ[/b][/size]

[b]Do I need modded exes?[/b]
Yes. DiegeticControl needs themrdemonized modded exes (20250908 or newer) or AOEngine (v0.55 or newer). Vanilla Anomaly does not expose the APIs it relies on.

[size=3][b]Credits:[/b][/size]
Altogolik - support, ideas, source materials

[line]

[size=3][b]Usage and License:[/b][/size]
Modpacks: allowed and encouraged. Keep the readme and license files.
Addons, patches, integrations: allowed. Credit "DiegeticControl by Damian Sirbu" visibly on your mod page.
Reproducing the implementation in other software: not allowed, even with credit.
Full license in LICENSE file and on GitHub.

[line]


[size=3][b]Reporting issues and suggestions[/b][/size]
Open a bug report or a suggestion at https://github.com/damiansirbu-stalker/DiegeticControl/issues/new/choose.
Also discussed on the GAMMA, EFP, Anomaly, and Zona Discord servers.

Before posting, read this readme and the MCM options.

Include:
[list]
[*]Exact steps to reproduce, from a new game or a named save, with expected and actual result.
[*]xray.log and the mod debug log (MCM log level DEBUG), plus engine build, modlist, load order.
[*]Describe the behavior. With hundreds of mods and overrides, only the log shows whether this mod was involved and what caused it.
[/list]
